<description>&lt;p&gt;Violent clashes continue across South Sudan, with government forces and SPLA-IO fighting in Wij-Panyikang, Upper Nile, and communal violence in Tonj North killing dozens. The government reported a 72‑person death toll in Tonj North, while victims of the Akol Koor residence clash are seeking over $340,000 in compensation from the Defence Ministry. Riek Machar denied commanding the White Army in court, and the South Sudan Bar Association launched a roadmap to improve access to justice. Canada emphasized media freedom as essential for peace, and the government and UN set a 2026 resettlement target after assisting 28,000 people since January. Two battle-related deaths were recorded in 2024, according to UCDP.&lt;/p&gt;&lt;p&gt;&lt;em&gt;Machine-written from the linked sources, checked for figures and names not in them.&lt;/em&gt;&lt;/p&gt;&lt;p&gt;&lt;a href=&quot;https://news.google.com/rss/articles/CBMigwFBVV95cUxNYkxCSzBha0hrWFFxMlI4VG82TjhDV2U2clNGQUxrX3JQUFRqanoya052V05YenhGVEVjT2VHdzM2elJQQV9FYjNicC14bHVuek5TRXRuSnVSaHZYQmxUalhMVi1pQzdsS1oyOG1aVnlmSGVwczBUaGYxU3Z3VTFWV1QxTQ?oc=5&quot;&gt;Sudans Post&lt;/a&gt;, &lt;a href=&quot;https://news.google.?oc=5&quot;&gt;Eye Radio&lt;/a&gt;, &lt;a href=&quot;https://news.google.?oc=5&quot;&gt;Eye Radio&lt;/a&gt;, &lt;a href=&quot;https://news.google.?oc=5&quot;&gt;Eye Radio&lt;/a&gt;, &lt;a href=&quot;https://news.google.?oc=5&quot;&gt;Eye Radio&lt;/a&gt;, &lt;a href=&quot;https://news.google.?oc=5&quot;&gt;Eye Radio&lt;/a&gt;, &lt;a href=&quot;https://news.google.?oc=5&quot;&gt;Eye Radio&lt;/a&gt;, &lt;a href=&quot;https://news.google.com/rss/articles/CBMigAFBVV95cUxQQWU3b0pmS2NwWE1kUjFZRUh2alhDdDFDMkREVHNvb2dIMHdsM2N4c1VFQXBLREVCV0xNMGdkSWdhTkxNWFdkek5VeWlOWlAyYlh0amtCVmU5cmxtRGs0cW1MSUxkdEdldm55ZWVUTGlVWnkwWE9NTy00eXc5LW1CWg?oc=5&quot;&gt;ChimpReports&lt;/a&gt;, &lt;a href=&quot;https://news.google.?oc=5&quot;&gt;Eye Radio&lt;/a&gt;, &lt;a href=&quot;https://news.google.?oc=5&quot;&gt;Eye Radio&lt;/